    "case_id": "553",
    "case_summary": "A male patient with initial presentation at age 18 years in 1984. Past medical history includes: a 10-cm mass of the organ of Zukerkandl (1984), right adrenalectomy (1987), followed by remission until 2014. In 2014, patient presented with palpitations and diaphoresis. In March 2021, patient experienced recurrence of hypertension. Patient had limited access to family history.\n\nIn 2021, patient presented with hypertension.\n\n- Laboratory Tests (2021):    - 24-hour urinary normetanephrine: 0.55 μmol/day (normal value <0.28 μmol/day)    - Metanephrine: undetectable    - Urinary 3-methoxytyramine: 0.22 μmol/day (normal <0.52)    - Serum prostatic-specific antigen: 0.42 μg/L (normal <4 μg/L)  - Genetic Testing:    - SDHB gene variant: c.338G>A (p.C113Y)  - Imaging Studies:    1. Gallium 68-DOTATATE PET scan (2021):       - Image Description: Shows a positive 1.7 × 2.1 × 3.8-cm nodule in the left adrenal bed and a separate focal abnormal activity in the prostate        2. CT scan findings:       - Prostatic lesion increased from 1.9 cm in 2014 to 2.9 cm in 2021  - Pathology:    - Immunohistochemistry results: Tumors positive for GATA3, tyrosine hydroxylase, chromogranin A, and synaptophysin    - Negative for low-molecular weight cytokeratin 'CAM5.2'    - S100-positive sustentacular cell network identified    - Lymph nodes: 0/2 involved",
